    <div class="about-col">
      <div class="about-col-title">The MYCIN CF Model</div>
      <p>Originally developed for medical diagnosis, the Certainty Factor model allows a rule-based system to reason under uncertainty — combining multiple weak pieces of evidence into a confident conclusion.</p>
      <p>CF values range from 0.0 (no confidence) to 1.0 (fully confident). The combination formula ensures that even imperfect evidence contributes meaningfully.</p>
      <div class="formula-box">
        <span class="formula-comment">// MYCIN Combination Formula</span><br>
        CF(H,E₁,E₂) =<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;CF₁ + CF₂ × (1 − CF₁)<br><br>
        <span class="formula-comment">// Where:</span><br>
        CF₁ = base keyword match score<br>
        CF₂ = rule-based certainty factor
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="about-col">
      <div class="about-col-title">NLP Pipeline</div>
      <p>The system performs lightweight NLP: lowercasing, punctuation stripping, tokenisation, and stop-word removal. Keywords and multi-word phrases are then matched against the knowledge base.</p>
      <p>Phrases score double (weight=2) vs single keywords (weight=1), ensuring "double charged" or "not delivered" carry more signal than generic words.</p>
      <p>Entity extraction uses regular expressions to pull Order IDs, currency amounts, email addresses, and Indian mobile numbers from the complaint text.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="about-col">
      <div class="about-col-title">Escalation Logic</div>
      <p>Three conditions trigger human escalation. First, if the combined CF is below 0.40 — the system lacks sufficient confidence and needs human review. Second, if the sentiment is ANGRY and the priority is HIGH — empathy from a human agent is recommended. Third, if priority is HIGH but CF is below 0.60, an agent verifies before acting.</p>
      <p>This three-tier logic ensures automated resolution for clear-cut cases while protecting customer experience in ambiguous or high-stakes situations.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
